      "note": "Embedded: resident growth per state, isolate, or Wasm module across 4 to 10,000 live sessions; Lua and LuaJIT run in a C host, the others in Node. Processes: memory charged to a cgroup per added process, above baseline, including the kernel's per-process memory; runtime code shared between processes is not counted. A forked CPython shares its warm parent's pages until it writes to them, so it grows as a script runs. Pyodide and MicroPython count as boundaries only with their JavaScript bridges locked down. Linux x86-64, 48 cores, load average 4 to 25 during the runs. Node 22.23.1, Deno 2.5.2, Bun 1.3.14, CPython 3.15.2, Lua 5.5.1, LuaJIT 2.1, bash 5.2, dash 0.5, isolated-vm 6.2, quickjs-emscripten 0.32, Pyodide 314.0.8, MicroPython 1.29. Not yet measured this way: CPython on WASI, Monty, PocketPy."
